  "scope": "Bounded paired Session comparison only: pinned SessionImpl through a driver subclass (guarded getter, recorded report) versus the private native session_core.Session in sync commit() and async acommit() modes, each over its real Memory backend; 41 closed scenarios and a closed DE02/DE02b cell map. Oracle adaptations: raw-base documents set checkpointWhen always true (every loaded change is written as a base) and createTask receives a structural task-definition stub. Native-only, never paired: adoption failure, reentry, every Task.cancel row, Tx/draft affinity, coroutine listeners, bulk queued-rejection timing, background-close reporter routing, a sync commit settling while its own inline backend close is held, process-control exceptions and sync callbacks returning awaitables. Not exercised: a caller mutating an entry draft's top-level keys while the append is pending (Pi reads them after its awaits, native at the call). Not compared at all: typed documents, migrations, families, task-scope documents and terminal-task document retirement, delta content and op-based no-ops, forks/copies, documentState/watchDoc, retention/eviction, unloadDocuments, telemetry and listener context, Harness hooks, SQLite. No product, factory, full Session parity or P-row closure."
}
